pdated_at":"2026-06-18T15:25:20Z","closed_at":"2026-06-18T15:25:20Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.beta1 and later 4.7 snapshots\nNot reproducible in 4.6.3.stable, 4.6.2.stable and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta1 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 17 May 2026 17:23:07 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13500HX (20 threads) - 15.33 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Surround 3.1)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf `LIGHT1_COLOR` or `LIGHT3_COLOR` are used in a Sky shader when the scene has less than 2 or 4 lights respectively, their values are non-zero, and affect the lighting of the scene.\n\nSky color set to LIGHT1_COLOR:\n<img width=\"1145\" height=\"641\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ca79a0c-a6f8-424f-8dd2-8d3a7c0b581d\" />\n\nOr LIGHT3_COLOR:\n<img width=\"1145\" height=\"641\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b33b0a9c-5851-475c-bfca-f286dde3bff4\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run the project with to observe how `LIGHT1_COLOR` affects lighting\n3. Replace `LIGHT1_COLOR` with `LIGHT3_COLOR` in sky.gdshader\n4. Delete DirectionalLight, the sky remains green when `LIGHT3_COLOR` is used\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[lightx-color.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28176027/lightx-color.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com